# Expectation record for 01_integer_conversions/001_usual_arithmetic_conversions.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_usual_arithmetic_conversions
area               = 01_integer_conversions
description        = Usual arithmetic conversions across mixed signedness and rank, folded and volatile-runtime
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every operand pair is converted under the usual arithmetic conversions to a common type
that represents both values, so no conversion is value-changing and no signed overflow can
arise.  The _Generic probes report the common type without evaluating their controlling
expression.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
fold_uint_common=4294967294
fold_ushort_promotes=-2
fold_uchar_promotes=-2
fold_llong_wins=0
fold_ullong_wins=5
run_uint_common=4294967294
run_ushort_promotes=-2
run_uchar_promotes=-2
run_llong_wins=0
run_ullong_wins=5
type_int_uint=unsigned int
type_ushort_int=int
type_uint_llong=long long
type_uint_ullong=unsigned long long
END
